#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# hazard_function

#% text
# `hazard_function(d, x)` gives the hazard rate of the distribution `d` at `x`: the density at `x` divided by the probability of a value at least `x` (`survival(d, x)` for a continuous distribution).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
hazard_function(exponential_distribution(l), 2)
#% output
#= l

#% cell
hazard_function(normal_distribution(0, 1), 1.)
#% output
#= 1.5251352761609813

